    "summary": "I couldn't build this as asked: the configurator won't let a drawer and a spike sit at the same corner of a cell. I put a half base at cell (1,0) with a drawer on its south cut face and added the cells around it. When I tried a spike at the south corner where (0,0), (1,0) and (0,1) meet, it was refused with SPIKE_CLASH (\"a drawer (south half) fills this corner of the junction, where the spike would stand\"). The drawer covers both south corners of that cell. As the nearest layout it accepts, the spike stands at the north corner of the same cell, where (0,0), (1,0) and (1,-1) meet. So the two parts share a cell but not a corner, and they don't touch. The joints are bolted. Capping the open faces was refused: one solid cap would run 5 mm into the drawer frame. So the 13 open faces are left uncapped (the check lists them as info, not errors). check_build shows no rule errors and the collision check is clear.",
